Why not have a pendant to the scroll of genocide that allows you to wipe 
out, instead of a species of monsters, a class of objects?

If it is blessed, it will eliminate any object that you indicate (say 
wands of lightning so going reflectionless becomes much less of a 
hassle), if uncursed, only objects that you have already identified. 
The fun part is, if it is cursed: you say "I want to get rid of potions 
of paralysis" and it wipes out *all* potions; no full healing, no holy 
water anymore...

This would open quite a number of new conduct challenges such as never 
using a tool (impossible unless you exempt the invocation ritual), a 
wand, a potion or spellbook (this is included already in illiteracy). 
Of course, certain items should be impossible to eliminate (e.g. all 
artifacts) but certain monsters cannot be genocided as well (the 
Chromatic dragon, etc.).  Eliminating tools too early would make the 
game unwinnable, since there would be no candles anymore (the 
Candelabrum would be exempt of course, but excluding ordinary candles is 
hard to justify...)
